# Claim before you edit

Four coding tools edit this tree: Cursor, Claude Code, OpenCode, Monkey Code.
Parallel edits on the same file have already caused truncation and a `git add -A`
sweep of another tool's work. So claim first.

```bash
python scripts/buzzlock.py status
python scripts/buzzlock.py claim <paths> --tool CURSOR --reason "<one line>"
# ... do the work ...
python scripts/buzzlock.py release <paths> --tool CURSOR --evidence "<exit code / tests>"
```

Use `--tool CURSOR` from Cursor. Claude Code uses `CLAUDE`, OpenCode `OPENCODE`,
Monkey Code `MONKEY`.

**Exit code 2 on claim means the file is held by another tool — stop, do not edit
it, pick different work.** A claim older than 4h is stale and can be taken with
`buzzlock.py break <path> --tool CURSOR`.

Registry: `docs/coordination/LOCKS.json`. Chat mirror: Buzz `#build`.
Full protocol: `~/.buzz/GUIDES/CODING_AGENT_PROTOCOL.md` ·
`docs/coordination/README.md`.

## Handoff

When you stop mid-task, post the handoff in `#build`:

```
[CURSOR] HANDOFF -> <next tool>
Goal / Done / Evidence / Left / Touched
```

A handoff with no Evidence line is a rumour, not a handoff.

## Never

Never `git add -A` — stage explicit paths. No commit/push/deploy without the owner
asking. Compliance gates (DND, TRAI window, consent, DPDP) are RED: weakening one is
an abort, not a fix. Swara/voice path is FROZEN.
